    "id": "p41-q21-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "21",
    "prompt": "Write $\\frac{67}{29}$ as a continued fraction. (See Exercise 2I, Question 9.)",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$2+\\cfrac{1}{3+\\cfrac{1}{4+\\cfrac12}}$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{67}{29}&=2+\\frac9{29}\\\\\\frac{29}{9}&=3+\\frac29\\\\\\frac92&=4+\\cfrac12.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute these reciprocal forms successively:\n$$\\frac{67}{29}=2+\\cfrac1{3+\\cfrac1{4+\\cfrac12}}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
